A||||6||k2m4||Starter problems||||1||
Z||000000||k2m4||07-12-2001||01:49 PM||||Hey Everyone! First off i wanted to say that i just recently found this place and im absolutely amazed! This place is a great resource!<BR>Now let me get to business...My 86 2M4 ive been having some starting  gremlins. Sometimes my pig after a hard drive wont turn over. The car acts like almost a dead battery.  I havent determined whether its heat related or not. The starter solenoid doesnt click engage ...nothing. Now i know you can take everything else in the ignition system away and it still should turn over.  But heres the kicker i can jump start the vehicle and vroom she turns over nice starter solenoid kicks in nice. Also this is super intermittent. Somtimes i can drive it hard and nothing and i drive it harder and get her real hot and shell start up like a champ!!?!! <BR>So heres my question Does any one think i may have a starter solenoid problem. i did notice that one of the terminals was really corroded down there. I cleaned it up it hasnt happened since BUT im still waiting for it to occur again...the intermittency of the problem before was too unpredictable. Any one have any comments, questions solutions, suggestions, anything ...<P>Kerm <BR>86 2M4<BR>86 1/2 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||Elenor84||07-12-2001||01:55 PM||||This exact same situation happended to me not to long ago...very iratic behavior of starting...once and a while it would do it and then it wouldn't...I would have to jump start it after I got gas!  Now thats embarising!  All I did was replace my starter and my battery...what I think your problem is and was mine is that inside your starter unit the wires are dangling...once and a while there will be enough connection and then other times there won't...I suggest u get a rebuilt starter(thats what I did)...fixed my problem completly.  Hope this helps...<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Joe Torma||07-12-2001||02:15 PM||||I worked on a 2m4 with a similar problem.  All I had to do was redo connections on all the wires at the starter solinoid and cleaned up the posts.  The years take their toll on the wires and connectors.<P>This may be the problem.<P>Joe||||reg||1
Z||000003||Leadfoot||07-12-2001||03:52 PM||||See if your gound is good.  I had the same symptoms.  The test is simple, next time your starter acts up take out your jumper cables and connect the negative terminal to the engine.  I used the exhaust manifold.  Make sure you have a good contact.  Then see if the starter works fine.  If it does then you need to clean the gound connections to the block.||||reg||1
Z||000004||starfighter007@msn.com||07-12-2001||09:05 PM||||I would put a new rebuild starter in .It is defeinitly a starter problem.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tigger||07-13-2001||01:30 AM||||Yep, check for loose/bad connections.  Still doesn't fix it, I'd say the solenoid is bad.<P>If it doesn't turn over like that and your stranded somewhere, give the solenoid & starter a good whack with a wrench or something.  Sometimes it'll wake it up<P>Get a rebuilt starter.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||k2m4||07-13-2001||09:22 AM||||hey guys thanks for all the info. i think it was just simple corroded terminals...I havent had any problems since. i pulled the starter cleaned it up . Made sure i had good ground. Checked voltages down there when cranking. Checked (bench tested) the starter solenoid. Cleaned up my battery terminals went through everything i could think of last night. If it does it again ill eat my own **** ...i think...LOL<P>kerm<BR>86 2M4<BR>86 1/2 GT||||reg||1
